erties of the schema, therefore no required‑property errors are emitted.'}]}, {'group': 'Recursive Anchor Handling (isRecursiveAnchor == true)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{"self": {"$ref": "#"}}'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult that does not enter infinite recursion and contains validation messages only for the outer object (e.g., no StackOverflowError)', 'description': 'When the schema is marked as a recursive anchor, the validator must recognise the `$ref` to itself and avoid endless recursion, returning a proper ValidationResult.'}]}, {'group': 'Keyword Walk Listener Invocation (keywordWalkListenerRunner != null)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{"title": "Example"}'}], 'expected': "ValidationResult where the mock WalkListenerRunner's `run` method has been called exactly once with the appropriate context", 'description': 'If a WalkListenerRunner is configured, `validateAndCollect` must invoke it during validation. The test verifies that the runner is called.'}]}, {'group': 'Schema Resource Root Shortcut (isSchemaResourceRoot == true)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{"id": "http://example.com/schema"}'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult that contains a ValidationMessage indicating that the schema resource root was used (or simply succeeds without extra processing)', 'description': 'When the schema is flagged as a resource root, the validator may apply special handling (e.g., base URI resolution). The test ensures this branch is exercised.'}]}, {'group': 'ExecutionContext Customizer Effects', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{"value": 10}'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult reflecting the modifications performed by a custom ExecutionContext (e.g., a custom format validator is added and triggers an extra ValidationMessage)', 'description': 'Passing a custom ExecutionContext (via the overloaded public method) can change validation behavior. This case verifies that the customizer’s effects are visible in the result.'}]}, {'group': '$ref Resolution to Internal Definition', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{"person": {"$ref": "#/definitions/name"}}'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult with no ValidationMessage because the $ref resolves to a definition that validates the referenced value (e.g., a string) correctly.', 'description': 'The schema contains a definition "name" of type string. The instance uses $ref to point to that definition. validateAndCollect should resolve the $ref and apply the referenced validators, resulting in a successful validation.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '{"person": {"$ref": "#/definitions/age"}}'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult containing a ValidationMessage indicating type mismatch (expected integer) because the referenced definition expects an integer but the instance provides an object.', 'description': 'The $ref resolves to a definition that expects an integer. The supplied node is an object, so the validator should report a type error after $ref resolution.'}]}, {'group': 'Enum Validation', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '"RED"'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult with empty ValidationMessage set because the value is one of the allowed enum values ["RED","GREEN","BLUE"].', 'description': 'The schema defines an enum of three colour strings. The instance supplies a matching value, so validation succeeds.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '"YELLOW"'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult containing a ValidationMessage stating that the value is not one of the allowed enum values.', 'description': 'The instance provides a value not present in the enum list, triggering an enum validation error.'}]}, {'group': 'Const Validation', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'node', 'value': '42'}], 'expected': 'ValidationResult with empty ValidationMessage set because the instance equals the const value defined in the schema.', 'description': 'The schema uses "const": 42